WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.467
-Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.367
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:05.901
Yeah, that feels good, right?

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.534
The aud--
-Oh, my goodness.

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:09.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
Guys, oh, my goodness.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.400
You make me feel so special.
Wow!

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.434
-You're beloved.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:17.567
-We love you as Ned.
-Oh, thank you, man.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:18.868
Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.300
Oh, thank you, guys.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.033
-You're funny. You're natural.
It's so good.

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.634
I just wanted to remind you --
I don't know if you know this --

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:25.067
you're in three of the top-10

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.934
highest-grossing movies
of all time.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.501
-Whoa!
-Come on, now.

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.367
-Whoa!
-Of all time.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:33.267
-That is honestly --
I can't even begin to explain

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.033
my excitement
just being on, Jimmy.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:38.534
I just want to say, I first came
out to the mainland

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.834
and I started going to
drama school back in 2015,

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.000
near the Flat Iron Building
downtown.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.234
-Yeah.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.767
-And, you know,
being a broke college student,

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.200
my friends and I --

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's 90% of our audience.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:54.067
-I appreciate you all.
-Yeah, me too.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:56.467
-The thing that we could afford
to do every day in New York

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.667
was to walk
up and down Manhattan.

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:01.734
So, to walk by
this building every day

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.501
and just hopefully
one day be on,

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.968
and to really
be on today is just --

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:09.434
My mind is --
I'm so, like -- It's insane.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:10.834
And The Roots --

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:13.601
Like, I literally am such a
big -- I can't even believe

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.133
I'm breathing the same air
as you guys.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.667
Like, this is crazy.
Oh, my goodness.

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:21.200
-Now we're family. Come on.
-Oh, I appreciate you.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.100
Thank you, Jimmy. Thank you.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.234
-"Spider-Man: Homecoming"
was only your second movie.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.968
-Yes, for sure.
-That's wild.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.767
-Yeah, some people
just get hella lucky.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:33.133
I don't know what it is.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.234
-I mean, and how did you
get chemistry with

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:36.334
Tom Holland that fast?

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:37.534
I mean, it feels like you guys

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:38.901
were really
best friends in --

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:41.033
-Yeah, I mean,
I'm very lucky that, you know,

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.300
we all sort of started
this journey together.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:46.000
We were both -- I mean,
we were all 19 at the time.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.801
And, so, you know,
putting a bunch of young kids

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:51.467
together on a movie is maybe not
be the most responsible idea.

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:52.667
But, you know, through that,

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.000
through all the
trial and tribulation,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.701
we've sort of just grown
together as, like, a family.

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:58.968
And now every day
is like just family day.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:01.434
-Yeah. Well, you --
-Yeah.

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:04.267
-You guys were roommates, right?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.634
-That's a fast way
to get to know someone.

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.367
-Yeah, for sure.
It was like a frat house.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.033
You know, like, a bunch of
19-year-olds

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:11.501
just, like, messing up
and eating a lot of junk food.

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:12.801
Not the best environment,

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:15.000
but the funnest environment
for sure.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.400
-You had to keep one of
the greatest secrets of all time

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.667
for "No Way Home."

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:23.334
You were in the scene with
all three Spider-Men.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:26.968
-Yep, classic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:29.367
Yeah, my --
This is actually really funny.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:31.901
But my girlfriend --
I had brought her on

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:34.467
to, like, visit work once,
and it was, like,

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:38.100
inadvertently during, like, when
Tobey and Andrew first came.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.901
And I had introduced her to
Tobey, and she was like, "Wait.

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:46.033
Why is this Spider-Man,
like, on your 'Spider-Man'?"

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.400
And I was like, "Well, baby,

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.267
it's, like, a really big secret,
so maybe don't say nothing."

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:51.534
Yeah.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:54.767
And she was like --
Like, she's not a big fan,

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.367
but she obviously
loves "Spider-Man."

00:02:56.367 --> 00:03:00.434
But I think that she
was going to tell her dad

00:03:00.434 --> 00:03:01.701
just, like, out of nowhere,
and I had to stop her.

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:03.167
-No.

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.968
-But, like, you know, her dad
wasn't going to say anything.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.133
I just feel like she's not

00:03:06.133 --> 00:03:07.200
really used to
this world, obviously.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.367
-No.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:09.834
-Yeah, so, she sat on it
for a year and a half.

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:13.567
She knew the secret
everyone wanted to know. Yeah.

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:14.767
-That's also
a bonding experience.

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:15.968
-Yeah, for sure.

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:18.634
She definitely got to know
them really quick.

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:22.634
-Yeah. Some fans think that your
character may become a villain

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:23.901
somewhere in the Multiverse.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:26.200
-Uh-huh. Interesting.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.033
You know, I'd just like to say,
I'm really sorry, everyone.

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:31.701
I did this really
stupid thing back in 2016

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:33.834
and mentioned it
in an interview.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:37.667
And then I stupidly just
continued with the story as if

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.400
like I knew
what was going to happen.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.234
And now everyone
is talking about it.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:45.033
And I just -- I'm sorry for
all the misinformation.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:46.667
-Wait.
What's the misinformation?

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:49.834
-I mean, like, there's just --
A lot of people like the idea,

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:52.400
and a lot of people
are disgusted by the idea.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.033
So I just feel like I --
Because I'm very much --

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:57.167
I'll do whatever.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:58.501
You know what I mean? But...

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:01.801
-I mean, clearly, we know that
you love Tom Holland.

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.801
You love Spider-Man. Of course.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:06.334
But a good story
is a good story.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:07.734
-Yeah.
-Nothing beats a good story.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.434
-It scares me
because "The Tonight Show"

00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:10.701
is a big deal,
and if I say something on

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.167
"The Tonight Show"...

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.901
[ Breathes deeply ]
-Okay, yeah, alright.

00:04:13.901 --> 00:04:15.067
Alright, yeah.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:17.968
But, hey,
if you guys want it enough,

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:20.234
let Marvel know,
and we'll figure something out.

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.400
-The fans will do it, you know?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.033
-Yeah, the fans
will make it happen.

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.567
And you want the fans
to watch your new series,

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:27.634
"Reginald the Vampire."

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:28.968
-Yes. Oh, please.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.834
-You star in this.
You executive-produced it.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:33.567
-Yeah.
-How do you describe this show?

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.801
-I would say it's something

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:38.367
that we've absolutely never
put on TV before.

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:41.534
I would say that it's
a very zany and quirky,

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:42.834
but lovable show.

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:45.100
You know, I think that
we have a lot of comparisons

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.767
to other shows, but I would say,
you guys just won't

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:50.667
expect what's going to
happen in the show.

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:55.200
-Yeah. It's in the vampire
world, but it's not --

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:57.767
-It's sort of like --
It's watching, like,

00:04:57.767 --> 00:05:00.300
a human being go through
all the human things,

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.968
like trying to
establish relationships

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:06.701
and finding a friend and finding
your place in the universe,

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:09.767
but all in the backdrop of
becoming a vampire.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:12.400
So it's a
very normal, human story.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.367
-It's relatable up to a point.
-Absolutely.

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.367
-Yeah, and it's fun. Yeah.
-Absolutely.

00:05:16.367 --> 00:05:18.200
-I do want to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.767
Here's Jacob Batalon
in "Reginald the Vampire."

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:21.901
Take a look at this.

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:23.767
-Oh, no.

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:27.300
No.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.234
Vampires are not real.

00:05:31.234 --> 00:05:32.434
They're just a story.

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:34.934
-Look, you're a
mother[bleep] vampire, man.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.133
You're -- You're undead.

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:39.100
You can never die...

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.734
never grow old.

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:42.667
I mean, you can't die
unless someone

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:45.000
stakes you in the heart
or you get stranded in the sun,

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.234
but that's very, very unlikely.

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:49.968
-Can I still eat pizza?

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:50.968
-Yeah, go for it.

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:52.200
You can eat pizza.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.767
-What about ice cream?
-Ice cream, too.

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.634
-So my taste buds still taste.

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:00.133
-I think you're putting
a little too much emphasis on

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:01.234
the pizza and
the ice cream right now.

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:05.434
-Yeah, exactly.
Jacob Batalon, everybody.

00:06:05.434 --> 00:06:10.200
"Reginald the Vampire" premieres
Wednesday at 10:00 p.m. on Syfy.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.667
We love you, bud.
-Appreciate you, Jimmy.

00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:13.767
-Justin Thomas
joins us after the break.

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:14.801
Stick around, everybody!

